{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Pandas Module 1 Practice\n",
        "\n",
        "### Dataset\n",
        "Titanic CSV\n",
        "\n",
        "### Goal\n",
        "Revise core Pandas operations by actually running them on the Titanic dataset.\n",
        "\n",
        "### My learning method\n",
        "For each important operation I will note:\n",
        "\n",
        "**Objective → Concept → Code → Output → My Observation → What I Learned**\n",
        "\n",
        "I am keeping this notebook as a learning record, not as a perfect notebook.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# 1. Load the Titanic CSV\n",
        "\n",
        "### Objective\n",
        "Read the Titanic CSV file and store it in a DataFrame.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Concept\n",
        "`pd.read_csv()` loads CSV data into a Pandas DataFrame.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "\n",
        "df = pd.read_csv(\"../01_Data/Titanic.csv\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Output\n",
        "There is no printed output because I only loaded the data into `df(DataFrame)`.\n",
        "\n",
        "### My Observation\n",
        "The data is now stored in `df`, so I can use Pandas operations on it.\n",
        "\n",
        "### What I Learned\n",
        "`read_csv()` is the starting point when the data is available as a CSV file.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# 2. `head()` — Look at the Beginning\n",
